From: BerryMC <148406068+BerryMC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:02:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fast-path hasEffect for entities without effects

EntityLiving.hasEffect is consulted on hot per-tick paths (breathing,
fire damage, potion applicability) for every living entity. Most
entities carry no potion effects, so guarding the HashMap lookup with
an isEmpty() check (a size read) skips the hash+probe entirely.
Behavior identical for any key containment result.

Based on Leaf's 'Optimize map lookups with isEmpty check' pattern.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/EntityLiving.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/EntityLiving.java
index 75c1681fc7b9dbb406758eae68d70f80810578b3..da3d272cf4a6c1e81e311635ed800bafcbd46460 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/EntityLiving.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/EntityLiving.java
@@ -689,7 +689,9 @@ public abstract class EntityLiving extends Entity {
     }
 
     public boolean hasEffect(MobEffectList mobeffectlist) {
-        return this.effects.containsKey(mobeffectlist);
+        // Dionysus start - most entities have no effects at all; skip the hash lookup
+        return !this.effects.isEmpty() && this.effects.containsKey(mobeffectlist);
+        // Dionysus end
     }
 
     @Nullable
